<article class="env-lemma" id="0F8T">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F8T">Lemma <span data-tag="0F8T">38.43.2</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0F8S" data-tag="0F8S">38.43.1</a> let $h : Y \to X$ be a morphism of schemes such that the pullback $E = h^{-1}D$ of $D$ is defined (Divisors, Definition <a href="/tag/01WV" data-tag="01WV">31.14.12</a>). Let $(U, A, f, M^\bullet )$ is an affine chart for $(X, D, M)$. Let $V = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B) \subset Y$ is an affine open with $h(V) \subset U$. Denote $g \in B$ the image of $f \in A$. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$(V, B, g, M^\bullet \otimes _ A B)$ is an affine chart for $(Y, E, Lh^*M)$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$I_ i(M^\bullet , f)B = I_ i(M^\bullet \otimes _ A B, g)$ in $B$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
if $(X, D, M)$ is a good triple, then $(Y, E, Lh^*M)$ is a good triple. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The first statement follows from the following observations: $g$ is a nonzerodivisor in $B$ which defines $E \cap V \subset V$ and $M^\bullet \otimes _ A B$ represents $M^\bullet \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} B$ and hence represents the pullback of $M$ to $V$ by Derived Categories of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/08DW" data-tag="08DW">36.3.8</a>. Part (2) follows from part (1) and More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0GSU" data-tag="0GSU">15.98.3</a>. Combined with More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0GSU" data-tag="0GSU">15.98.3</a> we conclude that the second statement of the lemma holds. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>